      "content": "It sounds like you might be experiencing a phenomenon related to low-frequency noise, often called infrasound. While systems are typically designed to operate below perceptible human hearing, certain mechanical vibrations can generate low-frequency hums that humans can feel physically. It's possible the building's HVAC or electronic systems are operating at a specific resonant frequency within your living space. You should report this to building management so they can check the operational frequencies and vibration dampening of the smart systems.",
